{
  "$schema": "https://unpkg.com/knip@6/schema.json",

  // oxlint and oxfmt are pinned here and invoked from the REPO ROOT, by tools/lint.sh and
  // tools/format.sh. Both tools read their config and ignore files from the current
  // directory only, and the configs live at the root, so root is the one cwd where they
  // behave correctly — while site/ is the one Bun project that gets installed, and so the
  // only place a version can be pinned. knip sees the half inside its scope and is right
  // that nothing in site/ imports them; the conclusion is what does not follow.
  //
  // This is the ONLY dependency entry here, and it is narrow on purpose: an
  // `ignoreDependencies` that grows by reflex is how a dead-code gate stops reporting dead
  // code.
  "ignoreDependencies": ["oxlint", "oxfmt"],

  // `tools/` is the same shape one level up: knip is right that nothing in site/ imports
  // the vendored design-token contract or its validator, and wrong about what follows. The
  // consumer is tools/design-tokens.test.ts at the REPO ROOT, outside this scope, and it
  // runs them for real against site/app/globals.css under `bun test tools/`.
  //
  // They sit inside site/ for one mechanical reason: the validator imports postcss, and Bun
  // resolves bare specifiers by walking up from the imported file. There is no root
  // package.json, so a copy beside its own test would find no node_modules at all.
  //
  // Narrow for the same reason as above — this ignores a directory that exists to be
  // byte-identical to an upstream copy, not a directory where dead code could hide.
  "ignore": ["tools/**"]

  // Scoped to site/ because this repo has no root package.json — three
  // independent projects share the checkout and each carries its own lockfile.
  //
  // contracts/ is deliberately out of scope. It is generated by
  // `cargo run -p xtask -- contract`, so an "unused export" there would be a
  // statement about the Rust contract rather than about dead TypeScript, and
  // knip would report the whole generated surface.
  //
  // No `entry` list, on purpose. knip's Next.js plugin already resolves
  // app-router conventions — page, layout, robots, sitemap — and hand-listing
  // them would silently disable the gate for that directory: everything named
  // becomes an entry, so a dead file among them could never be reported.
  //
  // No `ignoreDependencies` either. postcss and tailwind are loaded by name
  // from postcss.config.mjs rather than through an import knip can follow, and
  // it resolves them anyway; pre-emptively listing them would have been config
  // written against a problem this project does not have.
  //
  // The first run was not empty, which is the argument for the gate. It found
  // `useMDXComponents` in components/mdx.tsx — an alias of getMDXComponents
  // that nothing imported. It reads like a Next convention, but that
  // convention resolves `mdx-components.tsx` at the project root and this file
  // is not that path, so nothing picked it up implicitly. Removed after
  // confirming typecheck and `next build` stay green without it.
}
